D2 (long-horizon price reversal) INDEPENDENT-WINDOW DISCLOSURE -- read before trusting any Sharpe/DSR number this family produces. Usable point-in-time history for this family is 2925 trading days (MEMBERSHIP_DATA_START-gated: no formation may predate 2015-01-07), and each cohort holds for 756 trading days, so this replay contains only 3 truly STATISTICALLY INDEPENDENT non-overlapping 756-day window(s), plus a partial window covering 87% of one more -- call it 3-4 independent observations of this strategy's long-run behavior, corrected down from an earlier, retracted 7-8-window claim (see module docstring). This family forms OVERLAPPING quarterly cohorts (cohort_formation_days=63) for statistical POWER -- a smoother daily return stream and a larger nominal sample for the Sharpe/DSR calculation -- but overlapping cohorts share the same underlying price history and do NOT create additional independent long-run observations; the honest number of non-overlapping cycles this backtest can actually speak to is still 3-4, not the dozens of daily observations or the 12 staggered cohorts might otherwise suggest. This is a SEPARATE caution from the DSR's own n_trials=4 multiple-comparisons correction (run in this family's own, never-pooled screening call) -- neither substitutes for the other, and 4 trials is itself below deflated_sharpe.MIN_TRIALS_FOR_DSR (5), so the DSR correction proper will not even compute for this family; only PSR-vs-zero will.

